FerrionOS change to upstream RedoxFS (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 5ba45a6887374ab425326656a276bb3b62eba7dc after the existing recipe patches. Found by the deterministic simulation in sim/redoxfs (sim/redoxfs/run.sh replay FILE runs a replay).

Shrinking a file freed records only below old_size / record size, so the last partial record stayed allocated past the new end: every deleted file whose size was not a multiple of 128 KiB leaked that record for good, and bytes cut off by a truncate came back when the file grew again. Truncation now frees every record past the new end and zeroes the tail of the record (or inline data) it keeps.

Replay (seed 3): create /x2; write /x2 0 40057; unlink /x2 leaves 1 block neither free nor used. Without this patch 120 of 120 simulated seeds fail.
diff --git a/src/transaction.rs b/src/transaction.rs
index c7e3e0d..c360c7f 100644
--- a/src/transaction.rs
+++ b/src/transaction.rs
@@ -1864,11 +1864,26 @@ impl<'a, D: Disk> Transaction<'a, D> {
             assert_eq!(offset, size);
         } else if !node.data().has_inline_data() {
             // Deallocate records
-            for record in
-                (size.div_ceil(record_level.bytes())..old_size / record_level.bytes()).rev()
+            for record in (size.div_ceil(record_level.bytes())
+                ..old_size.div_ceil(record_level.bytes()))
+                .rev()
             {
                 self.remove_node_record_ptr(node, record)?;
             }
+            let tail = size % record_level.bytes();
+            if tail != 0 {
+                let end = min(old_size, size - tail + record_level.bytes());
+                assert!(end > size);
+                let zeroes = RecordRaw::empty(record_level).unwrap();
+                let mut offset = size;
+                self.write_node_inner_records(node, &mut offset, &zeroes[..(end - size) as usize])?;
+                assert_eq!(offset, end);
+            }
+        } else if let Some(inline_data) = node.data_mut().inline_data_mut() {
+            let end = min(old_size, inline_data.len() as u64);
+            if size < end {
+                inline_data[size as usize..end as usize].fill(0);
+            }
         }
 
         // Update size
